response:
The incident involves the distribution of the OUTSTEEL document-stealing malware and LOADJUMP downloader via a fake Ukrainian presidential administration website. The attack starts with emails containing Google redirect links pointing to the phishing site, which delivers malicious XLL files (LOADJUMP) and macro-enabled DOC files. LOADJUMP fetches and executes 0707a.exe, which drops and runs OUTSTEEL to collect files and send them to a remote C2 server.

